{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b6a6f6d0-6b6a-4e2a-9a1a-task-mgmt-backend",
    "name": "Task Management Backend \u2014 Full API",
    "description": "Full collection for the Task Management Backend: Auth, Users, Tasks, Dashboard, and Profile/Notifications, plus a health check.\n\n## Setup\n1. Import both this collection and the companion environment (`Task-Management-Local.postman_environment.json`), then select that environment top-right in Postman.\n2. Seed the database first if you haven't: `npm run seed` (or `docker compose exec app node seed/seed.js`). This creates an admin at `admin@example.com` / `Password@123` (already set as the environment defaults), plus 2 team leads and 5 developers.\n3. Run **Auth > Login** first. Its test script automatically saves the returned JWT into the `token` collection variable, and every other request is pre-configured to send it as `Authorization: Bearer {{token}}`.\n4. Run **Users (Admin) > Get Team Leads** and **Get Developers**, then copy an `_id` from each response into the `teamLeadId` / `developerId` environment variables \u2014 the Task-creation requests use those to assign work.\n5. Requests that create resources (Create User, Create Task, Add Comment) auto-save the returned `_id` into `{{userId}}` / `{{taskId}}` / `{{commentId}}` so the rest of the collection can chain off them without manual copy-pasting.\n\n## Base URL\n`base_url` defaults to `http://localhost:5000` (running the API directly / `npm run dev`). If you're running the full Docker Compose stack, switch it to `http://localhost` (port 80, through the Nginx load balancer) in the environment.\n\n## Notes\n- Auth also works via cookie (Postman stores the `token` cookie automatically after Login), but the Bearer header is used explicitly here so requests work identically outside a browser context.\n- Role-gated endpoints (marked ADMIN / TEAM_LEAD / DEVELOPER in each request's description) will return 403 if the logged-in user's role doesn't match.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
